@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy and your data";
}

<div class="col-lg-9">
    <h1 class="h3 mb-3">Privacy and your data</h1>
    <p class="lead text-muted">
        Chirograph exists for one purpose: letting anyone confirm that an employment letter is genuine, unaltered and
        still valid. It is designed around data minimisation and transparency, in line with India's Digital Personal
        Data Protection Act, 2023.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we keep</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>About employees:</strong> name, email address, role or designation, employment start and end dates,
            the type of letter, when it was issued, and a SHA-256 fingerprint of the stamped PDF. The stamped PDF itself
            is kept so the employee and the issuer can download it again. The unstamped upload is not kept.</li>
        <li><strong>About HR users:</strong> their work email address and role. No names, phone numbers or passwords.</li>
        <li><strong>About verifications:</strong> when a check happened, whether a file was compared and the result,
            and an organization name if the verifier chose to give one. We do not store IP addresses or device details.
            Files uploaded for checking are hashed in memory and never stored.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who sees what</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Anyone with a letter's link or QR code</strong> sees the issuer, its verified domain, the letter type,
            the employee's name, role, employment dates, the issue date and whether the letter was revoked (with the
            date). Not the employee's email address, and not the reason for a revocation. These pages are hidden from
            search engines.</li>
        <li><strong>The issuing organization</strong> sees its own letters and every verification of them.</li>
        <li><strong>The employee</strong> sees all letters issued to their email address, from any employer, with every
            verification and any revocation reason, at <a asp-page="/Me/Index">My documents</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your rights</h2>
    <p>
        You can see your data and its verification history at any time. For corrections or erasure of a letter's
        details, contact the organization that issued it: it decides what the letter says, and can revoke it. Chirograph
        acts on the issuing organization's behalf in holding these records.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Emails</h2>
    <p>
        We email only to deliver sign-in links, invitations, domain confirmations, issued letters and revocation notices.
        Every link works once and expires.
    </p>
</div>
